@rekram1-node I think the disconnect here comes from there being a "Permissions" subsection in the Agents section of the docs. This section has not been updated to align with this order priority.

 If you look here [https://opencode.ai/docs/agents/#permissions](https://opencode.ai/docs/agents/#permissions), you'll see [the example that I previously included](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/6856#issuecomment-3708694403), which does not follow the last-match-priority rule. At least, it doesn't read that way because the first two matches are basically useless as it stands right now (the `*` takes priority). 

https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/7041 should clarify

> Documentation clearly state `@general` as subagent, it makes sense you can't `@` a subagent, otherwise you need to make it of mode type `all` in the config:
> 
> "agent": {
>   "general": {
>     "mode": "all"
>   }
> },

In the docs usage of the general sub-agent through @ is explicitly mentioned. Also, explore  can be accessed through @ just fine. 

I aggre with @rekram1-node . It is confusing.

I have the issue even with BigPikle:

